## Deterministic Producer timeout-scan test correction — 2026-10-16

- A full default workspace run failed once in `request_reply::tests::callback_timeout_uses_java_housekeeping_initial_delay_and_period`; an isolated rerun passed. The test relied on Tokio's paused-time runtime not auto-advancing while awaiting an asynchronous send, so workspace scheduling could advance through the scanner's three-second first tick before the assertion.
- Reworked the test to start the scanner directly, insert two pending futures, and advance virtual time explicitly to 2s, 3s, and 4s. It now verifies the initial delay and one-second scan period without a live send path or busy-loop keepalive.
- PASS: isolated timeout-schedule test (0.00s), Producer all-target/all-feature strict Clippy, and `bash tests/stress/run-offline-smoke.sh` (16 cases × 3, including the corrected callback schedule test). The complete workspace gate is being rerun after this correction and the Message constructor alias change.

